schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Ethereum (2015) was the first blockchain capable of running smart contracts"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Nick Szabo coined the term "smart contract" in 1994, but the technology
    did not exist until Ethereum launched in 2015 as the first blockchain
    capable of running programs like this.
  evidence: >-
    Asserted directly in the article's opening section; article's References
    list Ethereum Foundation documentation (ethereum.org) generally, not a
    specific citation tied to this historical claim.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/smart-contracts-explained.md
  interpretation: >-
    Establishes the historical grounding for why smart contracts are treated
    as a distinct, comparatively recent (2015-onward) technology.
  uncertainty: >-
    Widely-repeated history in the Ethereum ecosystem; not independently
    re-verified against primary sources in this ingestion pass.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/smart-contracts-explained.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
